diff --git a/PRODUCT.md b/PRODUCT.md
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/PRODUCT.md
@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@
+# Mira student classroom product context
+
+## Register
+
+product
+
+## Users
+
+School-age learners entering a released Mira lesson through Student Web and its authenticated classroom gateway.
+
+## Product Purpose
+
+Help learners follow narration, explore interactive courseware, discuss ideas, and complete practice. Mira owns identity, course visibility, progress, and mastery; OpenMAIC owns classroom playback and discussion.
+
+## Brand Personality
+
+Warm, clear, playful. The student classroom continues the existing Mira Orbit presentation.
+
+## Anti-references
+
+Do not transplant the operator workbench or default OpenMAIC theme into the student experience. Avoid an administrative appearance and decoration that competes with the lesson.
+
+## Design Principles
+
+- Keep the learner's next action clear.
+- Keep classroom controls visually consistent across current and historical discussion.
+- Scope the student theme to classroom chrome; preserve authored lesson and whiteboard content.
+- Preserve meaningful status labels and the existing interaction flow.
+
+## Accessibility & Inclusion
+
+Maintain readable contrast, visible keyboard focus, and reduced-motion support. Early-primary flows use large type and at least 48 px touch targets, as required by Student Web instructions.
+
+## Existing references
+
+Context is derived from the integration README, Student Web AGENTS.md, and app/mira-student-orbit.css. The parent repository's product references continue to govern parent-facing surfaces.
